At sunrise the geese lifted from Earth, engines borrowed from dreams. Their wings cut starlight, honks echoing inside glass helmets. Captain Honk read constellations like rivers, guiding the flock past the Moon. Meteors flashed. Fear faded into ritual. Migration became orbit, orbit became home, and the birds learned that space, like sky, rewards those who fly together. They traced quiet paths between planets, counting time by wingbeats, trusting instinct over maps. Together. Always north. Honk!!ÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿ